INSERT INTO job_postings (category_id, company_name, title, location, salary_text, source_url, raw_text, status, posted_at) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM job_categories WHERE name = '数据分析师' LIMIT 1), '麦朗（上海）医疗器材贸易有限公司', 'Data Analyst - 质量数据分析师', '上海', NULL, NULL, '1. Responsibility
1.1. Process and Performance improvement
1) Analyze QC (Quality Controls), complaint and deviation trends with multiple variables including suppliers, defect types, product categories etc. to identify improvement opportunities
2) Work with key stake holders to establish and meet their analytic needs and the analytic needs of the organization
3) Gather and manage quality data across all supply chain for reporting and analytics
4) Develop actionable dashboards and reports to support the QC Operations
5) Suggest and lead process improvement initiatives addressing gaps
6) Execute the various outcome and predictive analytic studies that improves the performance of suppliers and overall QC operations
7) Management, maintenance, and design of integration strategies regarding eligibility and empanelment including data quality, reporting and retention initiatives.
8) Help the organization implement technology solutions, including managing the requirements of a project or program and communicating progress clearly to all stakeholders’ levels
9) Recommendation of action plans to the QC and Medline Corporate Quality to improve key performance indicators
1.2. Customer/ Stakeholder management
1) Creates positive relationships with stakeholders through the appropriate management of their expectations and agreed objectives
2) Ensure proper socialization and understanding of system initiatives
3) Support Change Management, ensure appropriate plan are in place to drive changes efficiently
4) Work with key stakeholders to ensure initiatives are prioritized and aligned with the Shanghai Office and Corporate Quality goals and objectives
1.3. Project Management
1) Apply project management and methodology standards
2) Define project scope, objectives, stakeholders, roles & responsibilities in collaboration with key stakeholders
3) Establish a communication schedule to update stakeholders of the trend data and improvement plans
4) Other projects or duties as assigned.
2. Required Skills and Experience
1) Bachelor’s Degree and 3+ years of related experience
2) Previous experience with data analysis is strongly preferred
3) High-level understanding of all aspects of supply chain processes
4) Very good knowledge of information systems and technology trend
5) Problem-solving aptitude
6) Excellent verbal and written communication skills in Mandarin and English
7) Exceptional leadership, interpersonal and influencing skills with all levels of employees, management and customer
8) Proficient in Microsoft Office.
9) Be able to work in a multi-task environment, have strong sense of urgency and excellent time management;
10) Maintain confidentiality well.', 'open', NULL);
INSERT INTO job_postings (category_id, company_name, title, location, salary_text, source_url, raw_text, status, posted_at) VALUES ((SELECT id FROM job_categories WHERE name = '数据分析师' LIMIT 1), '上海依视路光学有限公司', 'Data Scientist 电商数据分析', '上海-长宁区', '2.5-3万/月', NULL, 'Position Summary
As a Data Scientist, you will need to be involved in data-hub building process of Essilor group as well as our partnered companies. Build data solution and matrix to feed our performance-measurement and analytic applications. These applications will help Essilor group optimize the marketing investment, improve quality of our digital business, enlarge our brands’ consumer data pool and retention rate.
Main Responsbilities
Dataset preparation/data quality validation: Assist the database building process of Essilor group, help to enhance data structure and validate existing data’s quality throughout all small projects.
Manage and analyze large data sets: including Marketing data, Ecommerce operation data, Product data, Market competitor data, Consumer behavior and demographic data sets. Using advanced analytics tools to pro-actively identifying growth opportunities. From Essilor group perspective and ensure all our marketing activities meet KPIs. Provide insight from a data science perspective, removing obstacles and taking ownership to find creative solutions.
Programming & Modeling: Create efficient and reusable code to manipulate and analyze data. Help to build Statistical Modeling and diagnose, validate and improve the performance of the models. Build up multiple dimensions of reports which are user friendly to end readers.
Interpretation and communication of findings: Communicate effectively with internal and external stakeholders on analytic data processing. Closely work with Ecommerce/IT/Finance team to ensure data set well organized and cover enough user needs. Be able to resenting and communicating results to influence senior stakeholders, prove the result to senior stakeholders and try to apply these findings to partner companies.
Requirements
At least 2-3 years of analytic programming experience, preferably in consumer goods industry.
Ability to assess technical challenges and program solutions, and solve complex problems
Ability to work in a team environment and be flexible in taking on multiple projects
Strong experience of using Excel, Power BI, Tableau, etc.
Experience of coding in data manipulation and analysis using Python, SQL and/or SAS
Experience of using Cloud to perform large scale calculations, such as AWS, Google Cloud Platform or Microsoft Azure.
Experience in handling large and distributed datasets on Spark, Hadoop, Hive or Storm, etc.
Bachelor’s degree above (Information, Engineering, Statistics, Mathematics, IT, or Computer Science majors preferred)
Strong written English and oral communication skills', 'open', NULL);
